Classes (one row per oracle step; scripts/lib/compare_common.py judge):
  IDENTICAL          the full view equal: termination, stdout and every kept stderr line in
                     order; the oracle exited 0 (or, for a file check, the content or mode is
                     equal)
  KNOWN-GAP          equal only in the masked view: the line classes Blaze cannot match by
                     design (`probe masks`) replaced on both sides; the detail names the classes
  IDENTICAL-REDUCED  equal only in the messages view: exit code, stdout, and the sorted list of
                     the complete ERROR/WARNING/DEBUG/INFO/FAILED messages and build-result lines
  BOTH-FAILED        equal (in one of the views), but the oracle's step did not exit 0: equal
                     failures, listed, never matches (no step declares its failure)
  DIFFERENT          the termination differs, or no view is equal, or the step is missing
  NOT-PORTED         Blaze stopped at unported!(...)
  SKIPPED            not judged (recount: a transcript not anchored to the named binary)
The footer counts the classes over all steps, then separately for the steps that run the binary
